    "body": "After module cleanup, a single-phase extension retains its cached module pointer. If an embedding host calls the exported initializer again, it returns that module with its cached globals already cleared, which can crash the next function call. An embedding application can reach this state by finalizing and reinitializing the interpreter in the same process.\n\nReset the pointer after cleanup when module state is disabled. The srctree regression calls the cleanup callback through `PyModule_GetDef` to make the finalization ordering deterministic, calls the exported `PyInit_demo` initializer, and checks that it returns a new module with the expected global. It fails on master and passes with the fix.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
